Instances of grid pathfinding in the format of E. Burns, S. Lemons,
W. Ruml and R. Zhou, "Best-first heuristic search for multicore
machines", JAIR 39, 2010 [see GridBoard in include/PBeFS/astar/Grid.h].

ethan_unit_four-way_1, jordan_unit_four-way_100x100_1,
jordan_unit_four-way_500x500_1, jordan_life_four-way_500x500_1
           from src/grid of https://github.com/eaburns/pbnf; their row 0
           is the last line of the board (AStarBench --origin bottom).
grid_500-500-0.7_0
           from grid-pathfinding/500-500-0.7 of
           https://github.com/jinnaiyuu/combinatorial_instances, a board of
           500 x 500 cells each free with probability 0.7; its row 0 is the
           first line of the board (AStarBench --origin top).

The larger sets of the second repository (grid-gen: 500 x 500 cells with
probabilities 0.45 to 0.6, 1000 x 1000, 2000 x 2000 and 5000 x 5000) are
made by its generator grid-gen/grid_gen.cc, which draws each cell free with
the given probability and the start and the goal in the first and in the
last third of each side; the files it writes are read as this one.

